package-lock.json text eol=lf
*.webm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# App-icon assets predate the LFS catch-all above — they're
# stored in git as regular blobs, not LFS pointers. Without these
# exemptions, the LFS clean filter shows them as endlessly
# "modified" in the working tree (real binary in index, pointer
# in working tree) on every status / checkout. Path overrides
# tell git to treat these as plain binaries, matching how they
# actually live in the repo.
public/*.png            -filter -diff -merge
src-tauri/icons/*.png   -filter -diff -merge
src-tauri/gen/**/*.png  -filter -diff -merge

# The Earth basemap textures are deliberately plain blobs too,
# for a different reason than the icons above. Every node loads
# them — they are the globe's surface, not an optional extra — so
# how they fail matters more than the 18.5 MB they cost.
#
# LFS fails them twice. GitHub bills LFS bandwidth to the *parent*
# repository, so every fork's CI checkout would draw on upstream's
# quota — the same leeching that serving them from upstream's CDN
# used to cause, wearing a different vendor's name. And a clone
# without `git lfs pull` produces text files wearing `.jpg` names:
# the build passes, the deploy passes, and the globe comes up
# missing its stars.
#
# Plain blobs arrive with the clone, work air-gapped, need no
# override variable, and cannot show up as pointer stubs. The
# price is carrying them in history, which is why they are 2048 /
# 4096 / 8192 and not larger.
public/assets/basemaps/** -filter -diff -merge

# The luma-check bundle is a diagnostic, so how it fails matters more
# than the 90 KB it costs. Through LFS, a clone without `git lfs pull`
# serves text files wearing `.mp4` names, and the check then reports
# "no H.264 decoder" for every browser it is opened in — a confident
# wrong answer, which for a probe is worse than no answer. The Phase 0
# 8192x4096 frame is 78 KiB and the rest are ~3 KiB; flat bands
# compress to almost nothing, so plain blobs cost little here.
#
# They are already plain blobs in history — this pins that, rather than
# leaving it to whether the committer happened to have LFS installed.
public/luma-check/out/*.mp4 -filter -diff -merge

# Five more plain blobs under the catch-all, pinned for the same reason.
# History holds their real bytes while the catch-all says LFS, and that
# mismatch is not cosmetic. The clean filter turns each file into a
# pointer whenever git compares it, so any checkout with LFS installed
# shows them as permanently modified, and the next `git add -A` commits
# the pointer in place of the image. That happened to the screenshot
# fixture below on a feature branch. The gating smoke test uploads it
# from a checkout made without LFS, and would have been handed a
# 130-byte text file named `.png`.
#
# Each stays plain rather than moving into LFS:
#   - The screenshot fixtures and `equirect-sample.png` are read from
#     checkouts made without LFS. `visual-report.yml` uploads the
#     fixture and serves the sample to the catalog fixture, and
#     `stac-api.yml` runs the STAC test that loads the sample. The
#     fixture rule matches PNGs at any depth but never the whole
#     directory: `-diff` marks a file binary, and the fixtures are
#     mostly TypeScript. A fixture in another image format needs a
#     line of its own.
#   - The events-tab handoff images illustrate a design brief, about
#     190 KB between them.
#   - The Weblate QR code is 791 bytes. Its blob stays in history
#     however the file is tracked, so moving it into LFS would save
#     nothing, and would add one more object the poster deploy has to
#     find on the LFS server. Its five siblings being LFS pointers
#     costs nothing: the poster checks out with `lfs: true`.
scripts/screenshots/fixtures/**/*.png  -filter -diff -merge
public/assets/equirect-sample.png      -filter -diff -merge
docs/events-tab-handoff/images/*.png   -filter -diff -merge
poster/assets/qr/weblate.png           -filter -diff -merge
